 the same period of 2025 the price is 9.3% higher. For late September it is a high price: dearer than 84% of the comparable weeks of the last five years. Over the last twelve months Italy imported 25,291 tonnes, 53% of it from Norway, down 3% on the previous twelve.</p>\n  <table class=\"pir-tabella\">\n    <caption>Last twelve weeks. Statistics Norway (SSB), table 03024; converted to euro at the ECB reference rate of the same week.</caption>\n    <thead><tr><th>Week</th><th>€/kg</th><th>NOK/kg</th><th>Tonnes</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody><tr><td>2026-W28</td><td>8.27</td><td>95.15</td><td>13,914</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W29</td><td>8.46</td><td>97.43</td><td>14,283</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W30</td><td>8.08</td><td>93.23</td><td>15,138</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W31</td><td>7.40</td><td>84.10</td><td>14,640</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W32</td><td>6.90</td><td>78.69</td><td>15,555</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W33</td><td>6.91</td><td>78.47</td><td>16,232</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W34</td><td>6.77</td><td>77.01</td><td>19,254</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W35</td><td>6.86</td><td>77.90</td><td>19,200</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W36</td><td>6.42</td><td>72.90</td><td>18,639</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W37</td><td>6.74</td><td>75.80</td><td>20,991</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W38</td><td>6.80</td><td>76.43</td><td>21,141</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W39</td><td>6.68</td><td>75.55</td><td>20,078</td></tr></tbody>\n  </table>\n  <dl class=\"pir-domande\"><dt>Is this price high for the time of year?</dt><dd>The band at the top compares the week with the same weeks of the previous five years.</dd><dt>Is this the price my supplier is asking?</dt><dd>No. It is the average export value from Norway, across all sizes and destinations. It serves as a trend reference, not as a contractual quotation.</dd><dt>How much of it reaches Italy?</dt><dd>The flows panel shows monthly Italian imports and the rolling twelve-month total.</dd></dl>\n</section>"}